er-resources/registering-to-vote.htm . VOTE BY MAIL BALLOT APPLICATION REQUEST DEADLINE  - Tuesday, April 28, 2026 at 5 p.m. Completed Vote By Mail ballots must be received in the Town Clerk's Office no later than 8 p.m. on Election Day (Tuesday, May 5, 2026). For more information, contact Bill Oelfke, Town Clerk, at 978-425-2600 X1 or by e-mail at  clerk@shirley-ma.gov . Tuesday, September 1, 2026 - State Primary Election VOTE BY MAIL  - Vote By Mail Ballots will be available for this election.  Vote by Mail Ballot applications can be obtained by: (1) calling Town Clerk's Office at 978-425-2600 X1, or (2) e-mailing request for Vote by Mail Application to  clerk@shirley-ma.gov , or (3) printing them from website  https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/vote-by-mail-applications/Vote-by-Mail-Paper-Application-2025.pdf  .  If application form requested by phone or e-mail, the application form will be mailed to you.  Just complete the application form and either mail the completed application form back to Town Clerk, 7 Keady Way, Shirley, MA  01464 or drop them off at the office at 7 Keady Way in person.  Ballots for the September 1, 2026 Annual Town Election will be mailed out to those requesting them as soon as possible after ballots are available for mailing, which is typically in early to mid August 2026. EARLY IN PERSON VOTING  - Saturday, August 22, 2026 from 9 a.m. to 1 p.m. and Monday, August 24, 2026 through Thursday, August 27, 2026 from 9 a.m. to Noon at the Town Office Building, 7 Keady Way. VOTER REGISTRATION DEADLINE  - The deadline to register to vote to be able to vote at the September 1, 2026 State Primary Election, unless already registered to vote, is Saturday, August 22, 2026 from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. at Town Office Building.  To register to vote anytime, please visit the following website for information:    https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/voter-resources/registering-to-vote.htm . VOTE BY MAIL BALLOT APPLICATION REQUEST DEADLINE  - Tuesday, August 25, 2026 at 5 p.m. Completed Vote By Mail ballots must be received in the Town Clerk's Office no later than 8 p.m. on Election Day (Tuesday, September 1, 2026). For more information, contact Bill Oelfke, Town Clerk, at 978-425-2600 X1 or by e-mail at  clerk@shirley-ma.gov . 
     

 
